{"quote_id":"OOTW-CUR-001","corpus_id":"B007","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Out Of This World","source_year":1949,"source_slug":"out_of_this_world","source_section":"Chapter 1","quote_original":"The most remarkable feature of man’s future is its flexibility. It is determined by his attitudes rather than by his acts.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION"],"tags":["future","attitude","self-concept"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_out_of_this_world.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"OOTW-CUR-002","corpus_id":"B007","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Out Of This World","source_year":1949,"source_slug":"out_of_this_world","source_section":"Chapter 1","quote_original":"The cornerstone on which all things are based is man’s concept of himself.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","secondary_topics":["CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM"],"tags":["self-concept","cornerstone","identity"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_out_of_this_world.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"OOTW-CUR-003","corpus_id":"B007","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Out Of This World","source_year":1949,"source_slug":"out_of_this_world","source_section":"Chapter 1","quote_original":"All changes take place in consciousness.","primary_topic":"CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","secondary_topics":["SELF_CONCEPT"],"tags":["consciousness","change"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_out_of_this_world.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"OOTW-CUR-004","corpus_id":"B007","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Out Of This World","source_year":1949,"source_slug":"out_of_this_world","source_section":"Chapter 1","quote_original":"To cultivate the faculty of seeing the invisible, we should often deliberately disentangle our minds from the evidence of the senses and focus our attention on an invisible state, mentally feeling it and sensing it until it has all the distinctness of reality.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","secondary_topics":["ATTENTION"],"tags":["imagination","attention","senses","feeling"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_out_of_this_world.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"OOTW-CUR-005","corpus_id":"B007","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Out Of This World","source_year":1949,"source_slug":"out_of_this_world","source_section":"Chapter 1","quote_original":"Assumptions awaken what they affirm.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","secondary_topics":[],"tags":["assumption","affirmation"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_out_of_this_world.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"OOTW-CUR-006","corpus_id":"B007","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Out Of This World","source_year":1949,"source_slug":"out_of_this_world","source_section":"Chapter 1","quote_original":"I know of no clearer definition of the means by which we realize our desires than to experience in imagination what we would experience in the flesh were we to achieve our goal.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION"],"tags":["imagination","desire","fulfilled-end"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_out_of_this_world.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"OOTW-CUR-007","corpus_id":"B007","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Out Of This World","source_year":1949,"source_slug":"out_of_this_world","source_section":"Chapter 1","quote_original":"This experience of the end wills the means.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","secondary_topics":["IMAGINATION"],"tags":["end","means","wish-fulfilled"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_out_of_this_world.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"OOTW-CUR-008","corpus_id":"B007","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Out Of This World","source_year":1949,"source_slug":"out_of_this_world","source_section":"Chapter 1","quote_original":"The first step in changing the future is desire – that is: define your objective – know definitely what you want.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","secondary_topics":["DESIRE"],"tags":["desire","objective","clarity"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_out_of_this_world.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"OOTW-CUR-009","corpus_id":"B007","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Out Of This World","source_year":1949,"source_slug":"out_of_this_world","source_section":"Chapter 1","quote_original":"You must always participate in the imaginary action, not merely stand back and look on, but you must feel that you are actually performing the action so that the imaginary sensation is real to you.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","secondary_topics":["FEELING"],"tags":["imaginal-action","participation","feeling"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_out_of_this_world.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"OOTW-CUR-010","corpus_id":"B007","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Out Of This World","source_year":1949,"source_slug":"out_of_this_world","source_section":"Chapter 1","quote_original":"Instead, make elsewhere here, and the future now.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION"],"tags":["here-now","imaginal-action","present"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_out_of_this_world.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"OOTW-CUR-011","corpus_id":"B007","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Out Of This World","source_year":1949,"source_slug":"out_of_this_world","source_section":"Chapter 1","quote_original":"Experience has taught me to restrict the imaginary action, to condense the idea which is to be the object of our meditation into a single act, and to re-enact it over and over again until it has the feeling of reality.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","secondary_topics":["ATTENTION"],"tags":["single-act","repetition","meditation","feeling"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_out_of_this_world.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"OOTW-CUR-012","corpus_id":"B007","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Out Of This World","source_year":1949,"source_slug":"out_of_this_world","source_section":"Chapter 1","quote_original":"We must, with the minimum of effort, permeate the mind with the feeling of the wish fulfilled.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","secondary_topics":["FEELING"],"tags":["wish-fulfilled","effort","feeling"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_out_of_this_world.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"OOTW-CUR-013","corpus_id":"B007","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Out Of This World","source_year":1949,"source_slug":"out_of_this_world","source_section":"Chapter 2","quote_original":"Define your ideal and concentrate your attention upon the idea of identifying yourself with your ideal. Assume the feeling of being it, the feeling that would be yours were you already the embodiment of your ideal. Then live and act upon this conviction.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","secondary_topics":["SELF_CONCEPT","ATTENTION"],"tags":["ideal","attention","feeling","conviction"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_out_of_this_world.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"OOTW-CUR-014","corpus_id":"B007","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Out Of This World","source_year":1949,"source_slug":"out_of_this_world","source_section":"Chapter 2","quote_original":"In dialogues with yourself you are less inhibited and more sincere than in actual conversations with others, therefore the opportunity for self-analysis arises when you are surprised by your mental conversations with others.","primary_topic":"INNER_CONVERSATION","secondary_topics":["SELF_CONCEPT"],"tags":["inner-conversation","self-analysis","awareness"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_out_of_this_world.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"OOTW-CUR-015","corpus_id":"B007","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Out Of This World","source_year":1949,"source_slug":"out_of_this_world","source_section":"Chapter 2","quote_original":"You cannot continue desiring what you have already realized. Your desire is not something you labor to fulfill, it is recognizing something you already possess. It is assuming the feeling of being that which you desire to be. Believing and being are one.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","secondary_topics":["DESIRE","FEELING"],"tags":["desire","being","belief","wish-fulfilled"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_out_of_this_world.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"OOTW-CUR-016","corpus_id":"B007","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Out Of This World","source_year":1949,"source_slug":"out_of_this_world","source_section":"Chapter 3","quote_original":"Desire is the power imagination uses to fashion life about me as I fashion it within myself.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","secondary_topics":["DESIRE"],"tags":["desire","imagination","inner-world"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_out_of_this_world.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"OOTW-CUR-017","corpus_id":"B007","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Out Of This World","source_year":1949,"source_slug":"out_of_this_world","source_section":"Chapter 3","quote_original":"Look as though you saw; listen as though you heard; stretch forth your imaginary hand as though you touched…. And your assumptions will harden into facts.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION"],"tags":["seeing","hearing","touch","assumption"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_out_of_this_world.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"OOTW-CUR-018","corpus_id":"B007","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Out Of This World","source_year":1949,"source_slug":"out_of_this_world","source_section":"Chapter 4","quote_original":"It is our conception of ourselves which frees or constrains us, though it may use material agencies to achieve its purpose.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","secondary_topics":["REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES"],"tags":["self-concept","freedom","constraint"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_out_of_this_world.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"OOTW-CUR-019","corpus_id":"B007","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Out Of This World","source_year":1949,"source_slug":"out_of_this_world","source_section":"Chapter 4","quote_original":"Everything we do, unaccompanied by a change of consciousness, is but futile readjustment of surfaces.","primary_topic":"CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","secondary_topics":["SELF_CONCEPT"],"tags":["consciousness","change","action"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_out_of_this_world.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"OOTW-CUR-020","corpus_id":"B007","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Out Of This World","source_year":1949,"source_slug":"out_of_this_world","source_section":"Chapter 4","quote_original":"There is nothing to change but our concept of self.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","secondary_topics":["CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM"],"tags":["self-concept","change","identity"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_out_of_this_world.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
